=== QS001 profile: styleq | an underscore in a name, which is also the drop operator
some_name:1

=== clean profile: style | the same name says nothing outside the styleq profile
some_name:1

=== QS002 profile: styleq | a dot that is not a namespace
myspace.myvar:1

=== clean profile: styleq | a leading dot is a namespace, which is the spelling the guidance asks for
.myspace.myvar:1

=== QS003 profile: styleq | `l` reads as `1`
l:1

=== clean profile: styleq | a name long enough to read
len:1

=== clean profile: styleq | a name being read rather than assigned is not this file's choice
r:some_other_lib_call[1]

=== QS004 profile: styleq | a single token wrapped in parentheses
r:(1)+2

=== QS004 profile: styleq | a name likewise
r:(t)

=== clean profile: styleq | parentheses that group more than one token
r:(a+b)*c

=== clean profile: styleq | a call is not a parenthesised operand
r:g(1;2)

=== clean profile: styleq | drop reads as a token once its string is masked, and is not one
r:count (1_"abc")

=== QS007 profile: styleq | documentation naming a parameter the lambda does not take
/// Reads a folder.
//@param folderRoot The root.
readFolder:{[folderRoots] folderRoots}

=== clean profile: styleq | documentation that matches
/// Adds two numbers.
//@param a The first.
//@param b The second.
add2:{[a;b] a+b}

=== clean profile: styleq | a blank line separates the comment from the code
//@param x Something else entirely.

unrelated:{[val] val}

=== clean profile: styleq | prose with no tags is not checked
/// Adds two numbers.
sum2:{[a;b] a+b}

=== clean profile: styleq | a lambda with no declared signature has nothing to compare against
//@param x The argument.
implicit:{x+1}

=== QS008 profile: styleq | `x` declared somewhere q would not put it
f:{[t;x] t+x}

=== QS008 QF016 profile: styleq | further along a longer signature, and the rest go unread
f:{[a;b;c;x] x}

=== clean profile: styleq | `x` first and `y` second is where q puts them
f:{[x;y] x+y}

=== clean profile: styleq | `y` second alongside a named first parameter
f:{[a;y] a+y}

=== clean profile: styleq | no signature at all, so the implicit names are q's own
f:{x+y}

=== QS009 profile: styleq | `x` as a local beside named parameters
f:{[p;q] x:p+q; x}

=== clean profile: styleq | a local that is not one of q's argument names
f:{[p;q] r:p+q; r}

=== clean profile: styleq | a qSQL column alias is not a local
f:{[t] select y:a+b from t}

=== QS010 QS001 profile: styleq | a snake_case name in a file that otherwise writes camelCase
tradeCount:0
lastPrice:0n
get_trades:{[t] t}

=== QS010 profile: styleq | a snake_case parameter counts as a name the file chose
tradeCount:{[symList;start_time] symList,start_time}
lastPrice:0n

=== QS010 QS001 profile: styleq | one name joining words both ways
load_fooBar:1

=== QS010 profile: styleq | a PascalCase name among camelCase ones
tradeCount:0
lastPrice:0n
TradeBook:1

=== QS010 profile: styleq | on a tie the convention the file used first wins
TradeBook:1
tradeCount:0

=== QS010 profile: styleq | kebab-case is subtraction, and assigns only the last word
trade-count:5

=== QS010 profile: styleq | likewise at the start of a statement in a lambda
f:{[a] last-price:a; price}

=== clean profile: styleq | a subtraction that assigns nothing is just a subtraction
r:a-b

=== clean profile: styleq | a capitalised single word joins nothing
Date:1
tradeCount:0

=== QS010 profile: styleq | a function spelled in capitals borrows the constants' convention
GETDATA:{x}
MAXROWS:10

=== QS010 profile: styleq | a file written in Hungarian notation, and one name that is not
strName:"a"
symList:`a`b
dictKeys:`a`b!1 2
tradeCount:0

=== clean profile: styleq | functions carry no type prefix even in Hungarian code
strName:"a"
symList:`a`b
dictKeys:`a`b!1 2
getTrades:{x}

=== clean profile: styleq | a type-sounding first word in camelCase code is just a word
dictKeys:`a`b!1 2
tradeCount:0
lastPrice:0n

=== clean profile: styleq | capitals are for constants, which is the convention and not a mix
MAXROWS:1000
tradeCount:0

=== clean profile: styleq | single words join nothing
count1:0
px:1
tradeCount:2

=== clean profile: styleq | a qSQL column is the schema's name, not this file's
tradeCount:0
r:select total_qty:sum qty by sym from trades

=== clean profile: styleq | a table literal's columns likewise
tradeCount:0
t:([] some_col:1 2; b:3 4)

=== clean profile: style | the mix says nothing outside the styleq profile
tradeCount:0
lastPrice:0n
get_trades:1
